GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:19:**S2’s six predicates hold.** They are exactly the `if (idata` tests in `DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_ioc)`. Three accept one value (`W_MASK0` `{0x700000}`, `W_BASE1` `{0x240000000}`, `W_MASK1` `{0x3ff00000}`); three accept two (`IOC_CONF` `{0,1}`, `TB_ENA` `{0,0x80}`, `W_BASE0` `{0, 0x300800000}`).
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:25:**S4 is right about the machine, slightly overclaimed about the six arms.** `machine_alpha.c` adds `"lca"` only under `ST_ALPHABOOK1`. `lca_confwidth_probe.py` has driven a guest `stq` into `LCA_IOC_CONF` on stock `alphabook1`. That proves the **device window**. The other five labels are the same `DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_ioc)` at header offsets inside a `0x20000000` mapping — inferred from the switch, not measured. A miss at those offsets is still this handler (HAE at +0 is silent; `STAT0`/`STAT1` at +0x40/+0x60 hit `default:` and still kill).
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:35:**Do not split bitmask vs equality.** Five of the six fields are pure storage: `window_base_*`, `window_mask_*`, `tlb_enable` appear only as `odata = d->X` / `d->X = idata`. The sixth, `ioc_conf`, is consumed only as `bus = d->ioc_conf & 1` in `DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_pci_conf)`. Extra CONF bits are already discarded at the only consumer. A masked store (`idata & 1`) is an unlicensed extra under the addition licence; it is not required for correctness of anything that exists today.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:63:| **4 ACCEPT** | **This one.** Store already happened; five fields have no consumer; `ioc_conf` extra bits unused at `bus = d->ioc_conf & 1`; T_BASE siblings already accept; header encodings the whitelist rejects are documented (below). No latch: a message that says “unimplemented” about a value that stores and reads back is the footbridge wrong-record. |
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:112:`DEVINIT(lca)` registers the stubs on `%s.lca` and passes that path to `bus_isa_init`. `isa_interrupt_common` does `INTERRUPT_ASSERT(d->irq)` when PIC1 `irr & ~ier` **changes**. Construction does not currently fire them: PIC `ier`/`irr` start at 0, 8253 is `in_use=0`, WDC is only added if an IDE image exists, ns16550 asserts only with `com_ier` bits. The #506 probe’s legal session already survived on this machine. Opus’s 2026-08-31 note matches the source.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:133:Third, if someone “accepts” by deleting five equality kills and **keeping** `if (idata & ~1) exit(1)` on CONF: every window row stays green; only CONF-illegal rows would redden. Conditioning the remaining kill on a field the body reads (`d->ioc_conf` after the store is equivalent to `idata` — not a discriminator). The discriminating (d) forms here are **site omission** and **dropping one disjunct of a two-value predicate**, not an operand swap.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:143:2. **HAE (`case LCA_IOC_BASE`) already silently ignores writes** to a documented register. That is the file’s other “unimplemented register” disposition, and it is member 2, not 4. Do not unify it with the six in this patch.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:145:3. **`bus != 0` is not “non-zero bus number.”** It is `ioc_conf & 1` as PCI **cycle type**. The `else` does not assign `dev`. A later de-fatalisation that just deletes that `exit(1)` is an uninitialized `dev` handed to `bus_pci_setaddr`. Sketch it against the whole function when that round happens.
